## Lab overview

{{ m.overview }}

The **Model Context Protocol (MCP)** is an open standard that lets an AI agent discover and call tools. Databricks provides MCP servers for Genie, so any MCP client (your product's agent, an agent you write in Python, or a coding agent such as Claude Code or Cursor) can ask Genie a question in plain language and get back an answer, the SQL it ran, and the result.

!!! tip "Why not let the agent write SQL itself?"
    An agent that writes SQL against raw tables has to guess what "{{ t1.term }}" or "{{ t2.term }}" means, and it sees every table its credentials can reach. When it calls Genie instead, it gets the definitions you agreed in Step {{ N.sem }} and Step {{ N.agent }}, and Unity Catalog still checks the caller's permissions on every query.

