## Two MCP servers for Genie

| | Genie Agent MCP | Genie One MCP |
|---|---|---|
| Answers from | One curated Genie Agent: its Metric Views, instructions and examples | Everything you can access in the workspace, grounded in Genie Ontology (Metric Views, Domains, **Pages**) |
| URL | `https://<workspace-hostname>/api/2.0/mcp/genie/<space-id>` | `https://<workspace-hostname>/ai-gateway/mcp-services/system.ai.genie_one_mcp?o=<workspace-id>` |
| Tools | `query_space_<space-id>`, `poll_response_<space-id>` | `genie_ask`, `genie_poll_response`, `genie_get_query_result`, `genie_cancel_response` |
| Access | Permissions on the Genie Agent and its data | `EXECUTE` on `system.ai.genie_one_mcp`, plus permissions on the data |
| Unity Gateway | Calls **bypass** Unity Gateway | Calls go **through** Unity Gateway: grants, rate limits, policies, usage records |
| OAuth scope | `genie` | `ai-gateway` |
| Status | Public Preview (needs the **Managed MCP Servers** preview) | Generally available |
| Best for | A product feature scoped to one business area, such as the {{ s.genie_agent.team }} | Open questions and business-term definitions across the workspace |

Both servers are read-only. They query data and never write to your tables.

